          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CanadjinEh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yep, it's simple, just what I was looking for. Also, it's best not to ruin fresh tuna with too many strong flavours hiding it. Tasty and the husband really liked it - he's not really a fish fan. I didn't use nearly the amount of dressing that was called for as it's unnecessary. A couple tablespoons underneath the steaks in a flat pie plate and a tablespoon poured over the top of each and gently rubbed onto the edges too does fine. We didn't have anything to oil our grill with so used a grill basket (greased with a paper towel with EVOO on it). I also like Tuna a la Veracruzana, another easy option.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-23T03:16:29.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jan Miller"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I marinated the tuna steaks overnight and they literally \"melted in your mouth\". Good thing I made twice as many as I thought I needed because everyone wanted another!",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-20T16:00:42.640Z"
          }
